  "summary": "Added the environment-admin storage-capacity banner, driven only by the verdict the tenant runtime serves on GET /api/v1/usage/storage. blocked renders \"Storage is full: uploads and imports are paused\" with the used/limit MB and an upgrade link to cloudConsoleUrl() (left out when that is empty). warn renders the used/limit MB. ok, unknown, unlimited, non-2xx and off-contract payloads render nothing. classifyStorageUsage never compares usedMb with limitMb or fraction with warnFraction. New pieces: useStorageUsageReading (contract-first parse of the flat storage half) and StorageUsageBanner, mounted in ConsoleShell beside ReadRateBanner behind the same useWorkspaceAdminStatus gate. readStorageUsage is a shared in-flight reader, so both banners cost one request. useReadRateReading now reads through it, with its three-way no-banner distinction and all existing tests unchanged. Also added: five console.storageUsage.* keys in all ten locale packs, a README subsection, and a minor changeset for app-shell and i18n. No package-entry export, so Clause-2: no holds. Claim 5864158793 names this branch. Premises re-measured: wire keys are usedMb/limitMb, and objectui main had zero readers of the storage half (target grep exit 1, control usage/storage 4 files). No cloud field gap: StorageLimitRefusal declares details.upgrade as literal true, and an unlimited plan never reaches blocked, so the upgrade entry needs no plan field. useWorkspaceAdminStatus (org owner/admin membership, admin user.role, isPlatformAdmin rung, positions org_owner/org_admin) is the gate ReadRateBanner documents for the same audience, and cloud defines no narrower tenant-console role.",
